{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '2025,2065p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '360,460p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc | sed -n '555,700p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md | sed -n '500,565p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder_test.cljc | sed -n '275,355p;600,650p'\"","aggregated_output":"  2025\t           ;; leaked. Streams the composition supplied are never closed here;\n  2026\t           ;; their owner outlives this VM.\n  2027\t           pair-store\n  2028\t           (when pair?\n  2029\t             (let [created (atom [])]\n  2030\t               (try\n  2031\t                 (let [call-in (or supplied-in\n  2032\t                                   (let [h (create-stream! make-stream\n  2033\t                                                           capacity\n  2034\t                                                           :call-in)]\n  2035\t                                     (swap! created conj h)\n  2036\t                                     h))\n  2037\t                       call-out (or supplied-out\n  2038\t                                    (let [h (create-stream! make-stream\n  2039\t                                                            capacity\n  2040\t                                                            :call-out)]\n  2041\t                                      (swap! created conj h)\n  2042\t                                      h))]\n  2043\t                   {call-in-stream-key call-in,\n  2044\t                    call-out-stream-key call-out,\n  2045\t                    call-out-cursor-key (cursor-entry call-out-stream-key\n  2046\t                                                      (mint-oldest call-out\n  2047\t                                                                   :call-out))})\n  2048\t                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n  2049\t                   (doseq [h @created] (close-quietly h))\n  2050\t                   (throw e)))))]\n  2051\t       {:store {},\n  2052\t        :resources (cond-> (or pair-store {})\n  2053\t                     (:link-request opts)\n  2054\t                     (assoc :yin.link/request (:link-request opts))\n  2055\t                     (:link-response opts)\n  2056\t                     (assoc :yin.link/response (:link-response opts))),\n  2057\t        :origin (or (:origin opts) :t0),\n  2058\t        :ancestry (vec (:ancestry opts)),\n  2059\t        :capability-secret (:capability-secret opts),\n  2060\t        :secret-source (:secret-source opts),\n  2061\t        :attach-stream (:attach-stream opts),\n  2062\t        :parked {},\n  2063\t        :id-counter 0,\n  2064\t        :ready-queue [],\n  2065\t        :wait-set [],\n   360\t   answer envelope added are removed, nothing else.\"\n   361\t  [ans]\n   362\t  (dissoc ans :dao.stream.remote/id :dao.stream/identity))\n   363\t\n   364\t\n   365\t(defn- translated\n   366\t  \"A filed protocol error at the reflection: transport-error with the\n   367\t   error's name as the reason. not-found marks the reflection gone at\n   368\t   filing; no-surface and oversize mark nothing.\"\n   369\t  [e]\n   370\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   371\t   :dao.stream.remote/reason e})\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\t(defn- learn!\n   375\t  \"The attach probe's ok: record the source's descriptor and declared\n   376\t   surface, plus :closable.\"\n   377\t  [refl answer]\n   378\t  (swap! refl assoc\n   379\t         :source-descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor answer)\n   380\t         :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\n   381\t                        :closable)))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- install-more!\n   385\t  \"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\n   386\t   the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\n   387\t   reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\n   388\t   without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\n   389\t   identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\n   390\t   its own stream.\"\n   391\t  [link answer]\n   392\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)]\n   393\t    (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\n   394\t           more (:dao.stream.remote/more answer)]\n   395\t      (when (and cur (seq more))\n   396\t        (let [[o & further] more]\n   397\t          (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]] o)\n   398\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn- absorb!\n   402\t  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n   403\t   id is outstanding and whose identity is the outstanding entry's\n   404\t   reflection's own identity is taken: a not-found error marks the\n   405\t   reflection gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's\n   406\t   descriptor and declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is\n   407\t   emitted on the event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is\n   408\t   filed under its id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose\n   409\t   id is not outstanding, answers whose identity is not the\n   410\t   reflection's own -- a mismatch never completes a request, which\n   411\t   stays outstanding -- and values that are not well-formed answers,\n   412\t   are dropped as diagnostics.\"\n   413\t  [link v]\n   414\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n   415\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n   416\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   417\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n   418\t              req (:req entry)\n   419\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   420\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n   421\t          (when (= (:dao.stream/identity v) (:identity @refl))\n   422\t            (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   423\t            (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n   424\t            (cond\n   425\t              (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n   426\t              (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n   427\t                  (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   428\t                            (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n   429\t                    (emit! link v)))\n   430\t\n   431\t              (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   432\t              ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n   433\t              ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n   434\t              (when (nil? e)\n   435\t                (learn! refl v)\n   436\t                (emit! link v))\n   437\t\n   438\t              (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n   439\t              (emit! link v)\n   440\t\n   441\t              :else\n   442\t              (do (swap! link assoc-in\n   443\t                         [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\n   444\t                  (install-more! link v)))))))))\n   445\t\n   446\t\n   447\t(defn- channel-loss!\n   448\t  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n   449\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n   450\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n   451\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n   452\t  [link]\n   453\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n   454\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   455\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   456\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   457\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   458\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\n   459\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n   460\t\n   555\t\n   556\t(defn renewal-declaration\n   557\t  \"The explicit medium declaration of a renewal medium of `capacity`\n   558\t   (`dao.lease.md` Composition duties): a ring buffer evicting its\n   559\t   oldest at that bound, carrying portable values, attributing each fact\n   560\t   to its holder by the medium itself.\"\n   561\t  [capacity]\n   562\t  {:retention :evict-oldest\n   563\t   :capacity capacity\n   564\t   :value-domain :portable-values\n   565\t   :attribution :per-author-media})\n   566\t\n   567\t\n   568\t(defn- grant-for\n   569\t  \"The unsolicited grant for served identity `identity`, held by the\n   570\t   renewal medium `rid`.\"\n   571\t  [policy lease-id identity rid]\n   572\t  (lease/grant lease-id identity rid (::lease-duration policy)\n   573\t               (when-some [cap (::lease-max policy)]\n   574\t                 {:dao.lease/max cap})))\n   575\t\n   576\t\n   577\t(defn serve!\n   578\t  \"The UCF `serve!` callback (`yin.vm.ucf.remote`): `handle ->\n   579\t   {:dao.stream/identity id :dao.stream/channel descriptor}`, or nil\n   580\t   when this binding cannot serve `handle` -- the binding is closed,\n   581\t   the authority gate refuses, the surface policy refuses or names a\n   582\t   surface the handle lacks, or the capacity of live exports is\n   583\t   reached. A handle already live in this binding returns its one\n   584\t   identity and channel, with no second entry and no second lease. A\n   585\t   newly served handle gets a freshly minted identity, never one this\n   586\t   binding or any other has used, a fresh renewal medium entered in the\n   587\t   table with surface #{:writer}, and a lease granting the identity to\n   588\t   that medium's holder: the grant is queued on the judge, delivered to\n   589\t   the grantor's writer and seeded at the next pass, and the renewal\n   590\t   medium is wired to the judge under its own identity.\"\n   591\t  [binding handle]\n   592\t  (let [state (::state binding)\n   593\t        policy (::policy binding)\n   594\t        s @state]\n   595\t    (when-not (:closed? s)\n   596\t      (if-some [e (live-entry s handle)]\n   597\t        (served e)\n   598\t        (when-let [surface (and ((::admit? policy) handle)\n   599\t                                (servable-surface policy handle))]\n   600\t          (when (< (live-count s) (::capacity policy))\n   601\t            (when-some [medium (renewal-medium\n   602\t                                 (::lease-renewal-capacity policy))]\n   603\t              (let [lease-id (lease/mint-lease-id)\n   604\t                    rid (str (random-uuid))\n   605\t                    e {:handle handle\n   606\t                       :identity (str (random-uuid))\n   607\t                       :channel (::channel-descriptor binding)\n   608\t                       :surface surface\n   609\t                       :lease lease-id\n   610\t                       :renewal rid\n   611\t                       :renewal-handle (:handle medium)\n   612\t                       :status :live}\n   613\t                    g (grant-for policy lease-id (:identity e) rid)\n   614\t                    ;; wired through dao.lease's declared wiring, which\n   615\t                    ;; validates the declaration as make-judge does and\n   616\t                    ;; keeps it on the entry; computed before anything\n   617\t                    ;; is published, so a refusal publishes nothing\n   618\t                    j' (-> (:judge s)\n   619\t                           (lease/author-grant g)\n   620\t                           (lease/wire-declared-facts\n   621\t                             {:handle (:handle medium)\n   622\t                              :cursor (:cursor medium)\n   623\t                              :source rid\n   624\t                              :medium (renewal-declaration\n   625\t                                        (::lease-renewal-capacity policy))}))]\n   626\t                (swap! state\n   627\t                       #(-> %\n   628\t                            (update :registry conj e)\n   629\t                            (assoc-in [:table (:identity e)]\n   630\t                                      {:handle handle\n   631\t                                       :surface surface\n   632\t                                       :dao.lease/lease lease-id})\n   633\t                            (assoc-in [:table rid]\n   634\t                                      {:handle (:handle medium)\n   635\t                                       :surface #{:writer}\n   636\t                                       :dao.lease/lease lease-id})\n   637\t                            (assoc-in [:renewals rid]\n   638\t                                      {:lease lease-id\n   639\t                                       :handle (:handle medium)})\n   640\t                            (assoc :judge j')))\n   641\t                (served e)))))))))\n   642\t\n   643\t\n   644\t(defn serve-fn\n   645\t  \"`serve!` closed over `binding`, the one-argument shape\n   646\t   `yin.vm.ucf.remote` takes.\"\n   647\t  [binding]\n   648\t  (fn [handle] (serve! binding handle)))\n   649\t\n   650\t\n   651\t;; =============================================================================\n   652\t;; Retirement\n   653\t;; =============================================================================\n   654\t\n   655\t(defn retire!\n   656\t  \"The one retirement transition for served identity `identity` -- the\n   657\t   lease reclaim procedure is this same transition. First the identity\n   658\t   and its renewal entry leave the published table, so any later mirror\n   659\t   step answers a remote operation on either not-found; only then is\n   660\t   its entry released from the registry and its renewal medium closed.\n   661\t   Idempotent: an identity not live in this binding -- already retired,\n   662\t   or never served here -- retires nothing. A lease still in the\n   663\t   judge's ledger ends with cause :policy at its next pass. Returns\n   664\t   `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok ::retired? bool}`.\"\n   665\t  [binding identity]\n   666\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   667\t   ::retired? (retire-in! (::state binding) identity)})\n   668\t\n   669\t\n   670\t(defn close!\n   671\t  \"Retire every live entry and unpublish `lease-grants`, then close the\n   672\t   channel writer when it is\n   673\t   closable: the remote peer's channel reader answers end, and its link\n   674\t   reports every append! still outstanding as append-unknown -- the\n   675\t   transport's own close/loss path, nothing settled silently. Closing\n   676\t   the writer is the binding's to do only because of the ownership\n   677\t   contract `open!` required (::channel-exclusive?): the channel end is\n   678\t   dedicated to this binding, so no other reflection or mirror loses\n   679\t   its channel with it. The leases are not recorded here: each ends\n   680\t   with cause :policy at the next judge pass, which `step` still runs\n   681\t   after close. Idempotent; afterwards `serve!` answers nil and `step`\n   682\t   answers closed.\"\n   683\t  [binding]\n   684\t  (let [state (::state binding)]\n   685\t    (when-not (:closed? @state)\n   686\t      (swap! state assoc :closed? true)\n   687\t      (doseq [e (:registry @state)]\n   688\t        (retire-in! state (:identity e)))\n   689\t      (swap! state (fn [s] (update s :table dissoc (:grants s))))\n   690\t      (let [w (:writer (:channel @state))]\n   691\t        (when (stream/closable? w)\n   692\t          (stream/close! w))))\n   693\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))\n   694\t\n   695\t\n   696\t;; =============================================================================\n   697\t;; The drive\n   698\t;; =============================================================================\n   699\t\n   700\t(defn- budgeted-reader\n   500\tcontent lookup take (implementation plan, section 1). The meeting board and\n   501\tthe relay pair are section 4's instances of it.\n   502\t\n   503\t**Peer names.** A name is a self-certifying hash of a public key, the\n   504\tkickoff-hash form of `dao.stream.discovery.md`. It appears only inside\n   505\tconvention payloads. Nothing authenticates it until authentication exists.\n   506\t\n   507\t## 6. Lease integration\n   508\t\n   509\tA served stream is a network resource, so its lifetime beyond one call is\n   510\tgoverned by `dao.lease.md`. The judge is composed inside the peer that\n   511\tpossesses the resource, as that contract requires. What a lease governs:\n   512\t\n   513\t- A table entry a peer serves by its own policy: no lease; the peer retires\n   514\t  it when it likes.\n   515\t- A table entry served for a remote party (a stream a migrated continuation\n   516\t  still reads): yes; the remote party holds it, the holding peer grants and\n   517\t  judges, the identity is the subject.\n   518\t- A relay pair on a meeting peer: yes; the requesting peer holds it, the\n   519\t  meeting peer grants and judges, the two identities are the subject.\n   520\t- Link state, UDP reassembly buffers, channel sockets: no; governed by close\n   521\t  or by a bounded buffer.\n   522\t- NAT mappings and punch state: no; possessed by the NAT box, so no judge\n   523\t  can exist, and keep-alive cadence is the peer's own (section 4).\n   524\t- Board postings: no; records under the board's retention, each carrying the\n   525\t  lease id of the registration or pair it belongs to, and a reader treats a\n   526\t  posting whose lease has a `:lapsed` on the board as stale.\n   527\t\n   528\t**Mechanism: no new wire shape.** A grantor enters two conventional streams\n   529\tin its table, `lease-proposals` with surface `#{:writer}` and\n   530\t`lease-grants` with surface `#{:reader}`, published as remote descriptors\n   531\tbeside its meeting descriptors. A holder appends a proposal through a\n   532\treflection on the first and reads its grant through a reflection on the\n   533\tsecond. The grant creates one more table entry, a ring buffer with surface\n   534\t`#{:writer}`, and names its identity as `:dao.lease/holder`: this is the\n   535\tholder's **renewal medium**, and whatever lands on it is attributed to the\n   536\tholder by the medium, the attribution resolver `dao.lease.md` names as\n   537\tper-author media. The judge reads it with a local cursor. The renewal\n   538\tmedium lives and dies with its lease; the reclaim procedure removes the\n   539\tsubject entries and the renewal entry together, idempotently, and reports\n   540\tsuccess. A table entry under lease carries `:dao.lease/lease L`.\n   541\t\n   542\tUntil ShiBi exists, a renewal medium is reachable by anyone who learns its\n   543\tdescriptor and accepts a third party's renewal, extending a lease it does\n   544\tnot hold: attribution needs no credential, extension may want one, and a\n   545\tcomposition that must not accept it composes a gate on the renewal entry.\n   546\t\n   547\t**Renewal.** `append!` of `{:dao.lease/event :dao.lease/renewal\n   548\t:dao.lease/lease L}` on the holder's reflection of its renewal medium. The\n   549\treflection's `ok` is outbound acceptance only; the holder advances its\n   550\trenewal bound only on the source's `ok` observed on the link's event\n   551\twriter. A holder with no event writer stops at its bound early, never late.\n   552\t\n   553\t**Reclaim observed.** The mirror answers the `not-found` protocol error for\n   554\ta reclaimed identity and the reflection marks itself gone (2.4). The holder\n   555\tmay also read the grantor's own `:lapsed` record through its reflection on\n   556\t`lease-grants`: that is observing the grantor's stream, not carriage. And\n   557\tthe holder stops at its own bound regardless.\n   558\t\n   559\t**Expiry versus channel loss.** Channel loss is the absence of answers or\n   560\tthe channel's `end` (2.4); the table entry persists, so a holder that\n   561\treconnects within duration plus tolerance finds its entry, its cursors and\n   562\tits lease intact. Expiry is a present answer, the `not-found` error, on a\n   563\thealthy channel. Only expiry frees anything. A meeting peer that restarts\n   564\tloses its table and ledger, so every pair is gone, holders observe\n   565\t`not-found` and re-propose; this is `dao.lease.md`'s reclaim-and-regrant\n   275\t                       :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity}))\n   276\t\n   277\t\n   278\t(defn- remote-vm\n   279\t  \"A real semantic VM on peer A whose FFI call pair is two reflections\n   280\t   of B's served endpoint, and NO bridge: every call it makes is\n   281\t   answered at B or not at all. call-in is seen through `seen`, which\n   282\t   notes each value the VM appends. The call-out cursor the VM mints\n   283\t   at construction is asked for first, B driven until it is filed.\"\n   284\t  [pa pb seen]\n   285\t  (let [ep (endpoint pb)\n   286\t        in (reflect pa (apply2/endpoint-request ep))\n   287\t        out (reflect pa (apply2/endpoint-response ep))]\n   288\t    (poll! pb #(stream/cursor out :dao.stream/oldest))\n   289\t    {:in in, :out out,\n   290\t     :vm (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream make-ring-stream\n   291\t                              :capability-secret secret\n   292\t                              :call-in (recording in seen)\n   293\t                              :call-out out})}))\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\t(defn- lit\n   297\t  [v]\n   298\t  {:type :literal, :value v})\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t(defn- call-node\n   302\t  [op & args]\n   303\t  {:type :dao.stream.apply/call, :op op, :operands (mapv lit args)})\n   304\t\n   305\t\n   306\t(defn- load-call\n   307\t  [machine ast]\n   308\t  (load-ast machine (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\t(defn- settle\n   312\t  \"Run `machine` until it halts or 12 drive rounds pass.\"\n   313\t  [pb machine]\n   314\t  (loop [v (vm/run machine)\n   315\t         n 0]\n   316\t    (if (and (vm/blocked? v) (< n 12))\n   317\t      (do (drive! pb) (recur (vm/run v) (inc n)))\n   318\t      v)))\n   319\t\n   320\t\n   321\t(defn- raised\n   322\t  \"The exception `thunk` raised, or nil.\"\n   323\t  [thunk]\n   324\t  (try (thunk) nil\n   325\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e e)))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- apply-error\n   329\t  \"The portable apply error `call-result` raised, found on `e` or its\n   330\t   causes.\"\n   331\t  [e]\n   332\t  (loop [e e]\n   333\t    (when e\n   334\t      (or (:error (ex-data e))\n   335\t          (recur (ex-cause e))))))\n   336\t\n   337\t\n   338\t(defn- messages\n   339\t  [e]\n   340\t  (loop [e e\n   341\t         acc []]\n   342\t    (if e (recur (ex-cause e) (conj acc (ex-message e))) acc)))\n   343\t\n   344\t\n   345\t;; =============================================================================\n   346\t;; 1. Real VM end to end\n   347\t;; =============================================================================\n   348\t\n   349\t(deftest a-real-vm-call-is-answered-remotely\n   350\t  (let [t (channel)\n   351\t        pb (peer-b t)\n   352\t        pa (peer-a (:a-end t))\n   353\t        seen (atom [])\n   354\t        {machine :vm} (remote-vm pa pb seen)\n   355\t        parked (vm/run (load-call machine (call-node :op/add 1 2)))\n   600\t      (is (some #{\"Stream read failed\"} (messages e))))\n   601\t    (is (= :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone\n   602\t           (:dao.stream.remote/reason\n   603\t             (stream/cursor out :dao.stream/newest)))\n   604\t        \"the link is gone: its reflection answers channel-gone to any\n   605\t         op no filed answer covers\")))\n   606\t\n   607\t\n   608\t;; =============================================================================\n   609\t;; 6. Detach and rebind\n   610\t;; =============================================================================\n   611\t\n   612\t(deftest detach-and-rebind-under-the-same-identity\n   613\t  (let [t (channel)\n   614\t        pb (peer-b t)\n   615\t        b (:binding pb)\n   616\t        ep (endpoint pb)\n   617\t        ids (mapv :dao.stream/identity [(apply2/endpoint-request ep)\n   618\t                                        (apply2/endpoint-response ep)])\n   619\t        pa (peer-a (:a-end t))\n   620\t        {machine :vm} (remote-vm pa pb (atom []))\n   621\t        first-done (settle pb (load-call machine (call-node :op/add 1 2)))]\n   622\t    (is (= 3 (vm/value first-done)))\n   623\t    (stream/close! (:ab t))\n   624\t    (testing \"the channel ends: detached, entry and lease live\"\n   625\t      (is (true? (::rs/detached? (rs/step b))))\n   626\t      (is (every? #(rs/served? b %) ids))\n   627\t      (is (every? #(some? (rs/lease-of b %)) ids)))\n   628\t    (let [t2 (channel)\n   629\t          _ (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n   630\t                   (rs/reattach! b (:b-end t2))))\n   631\t          pa2 (peer-a (:a-end t2))\n   632\t          ;; the same VM rebinds its pair: fresh reflections of the SAME\n   633\t          ;; served identities through the new channel, its call-out\n   634\t          ;; cursor cell kept past the response it already read\n   635\t          rebound (merge (:resources first-done)\n   636\t                         {vm/call-in-stream-key\n   637\t                          (reflect pa2 (apply2/endpoint-request ep))\n   638\t                          vm/call-out-stream-key\n   639\t                          (reflect pa2 (apply2/endpoint-response ep))})\n   640\t          done (settle pb (-> first-done\n   641\t                              (assoc :resources rebound)\n   642\t                              (load-call (call-node :op/add 10 20))))]\n   643\t      (testing \"a subsequent call completes under the same identities\"\n   644\t        (is (= ep (endpoint pb)) \"the one endpoint\")\n   645\t        (is (= 30 (vm/value done)))\n   646\t        (is (= 2 @(:runs pb)))\n   647\t        (is (every? #(rs/served? b %) ids))))))\n   648\t\n   649\t\n   650\t;; =============================================================================\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-28 16:12:41 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 23:12:41 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**P1 | [yin.vm.cljc:2045](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:2045), [ffi.cljc:94](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:94) |** A fresh VM starts reading call-out at `:oldest`, mints its own call IDs from zero, and accepts a response by ID alone. The implementer reproduced a second VM accepting the first VM’s result. The exported endpoint does not enforce the stated one-caller-per-pair mitigation. **Fix:** ask the Architect to choose a correlation scheme that distinguishes VM calls across callers, or make an exclusive caller tenure an enforced part of the composition before calling remote FFI complete. Add a two-VM regression test.\n\n**P2 | [holder.cljc:213](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/holder.cljc:213) |** A `lease-grants` cursor gap falls through to an unchanged holder state. Every later step retries the same gapped cursor, so the holder never observes its grant or reports that it was lost. **Fix:** make gap an explicit terminal loss outcome and test an evicted grant.\n\n**P2 | [yin.vm.cljc:2045](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:2045), [responder_test.cljc:278](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder_test.cljc:278) |** VM construction needs a synchronous call-out cursor, while a reflection’s first cursor answer can be retry. Only the test helper performs the required pre-poll. **Fix:** provide and document a production readiness step that obtains and files the cursor before VM construction, or make VM construction handle retry explicitly.\n\n**Q1–Q5:** Q1 is a blocking correctness defect requiring an Architect decision on the fix. Q2 needs a production guard. Q3’s generic malformed-envelope exception is terminal, but it obscures known request loss; use a specific port